@@ -54,3 +54,12 @@ Tests use simulated hubs and temporary settings, without contacting lights or in
 Hardware transmission and reception still need to be checked with the Mini.
 
 The Acer preset comes from the [exact H6510BD model record](https://github.com/pickysysadmin/logitech-harmony-ir-archive/blob/main/devices/Acer/H6510BD.json) and its [published Harmony code set](https://github.com/pickysysadmin/logitech-harmony-ir-archive/blob/main/codesets/5b/5b0b82bf412b05cc.json). Original Pronto timings and source identity are retained in `assets/acer-h6510bd.json`. Menu is `0x10C821DE` in that archive's notation; Power is a toggle. These are published candidates, not physically verified codes.
+
+
+### 0.2.0 — 2026-11-27
+
+- Added the native Android app in `android/`, retaining bulb/room controls, advanced routines, presence, audio-reactive brightness, infrared learning/remotes, and diagnostics. See `android/README.md` for build and pairing instructions.
+- Added private HTTPS phone sync with certificate pinning and a per-installation pairing token. Open **Phone sync** in the desktop menu and copy the pairing code to Android Settings. Python 3 and the OpenSSL command are required; the listener uses TCP 43829 while the desktop app is open.
+- Routines synchronize in both directions with stable IDs, atomic writes, and conflict copies instead of silently discarding concurrent edits. One selected device executes shared schedules.
+- Refresh bulb states automatically every 30 seconds, discover new account bulbs every two minutes, and request a refresh after the other app sends a light command. Existing Govee bulb onboarding remains in Govee Home.
+- Preserve the existing desktop PulseAudio capture, routines, presence controls and infrared diagnostics. WireGuard can use the desktop and Mini's routed LAN addresses; broadcast hub discovery stays local.
